\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Keywords\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Keyword optimization comes down to the following:
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pause poor performing keywords\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Add new keywords from search query report\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Add new negative keywords\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 When to pause poor performing keywords?
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 There is no hard rule here but you\'92ll know a loser when you see a loser. If a keyword has had 100s of clicks and is showing significantly lower conv. rate and is significantly below goal then you are probably better off pausing.\

\f0\b \strokec2 When to add new keywords?
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
If a search term has at least 30 impressions per day month (1 per day) and has had shown signs of good performance then I like to add and test these keywords.\

\f0\b \strokec2 What match type to add new keywords in?
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
If you are using all broad match keywords successfully then add new keywords in all broad match.\
I also like adding top performing keywords in exact match form to see my impression share metrics - this doesn\'92t always mean exact match of the keyword will perform well but I like to give them a test.\
If you are not using broad match keywords fully and you are using phrase and exact then continue to add keywords in exact match or phrase match.\

